{
  "id": "policies",
  "version": "1.0",
  "title": "Policies",
  "description": "Standing work the tower starts at its slots: a markdown file with a json header and the prose a run starts on.",
  "requires": {
    "tower": "1.156"
  },
  "server": "server.ts",
  "client": "client",
  "views": {
    "policies": {
      "module": "view.js",
      "export": "mount",
      "on": [
        "floor"
      ],
      "scales": [
        "pane"
      ],
      "needs": [
        "display",
        "toast"
      ],
      "words": {
        "label": "Policies",
        "hint": "standing work the tower runs at its slots: rules, standing, Run now and Approve"
      }
    },
    "tray": {
      "module": "tray.js",
      "export": "mount",
      "on": [
        "collection.policies"
      ],
      "scales": [
        "row"
      ],
      "needs": [
        "display"
      ],
      "words": {
        "label": "Policies",
        "hint": "the floor's policies counted, with what is offered and what needs you"
      }
    }
  },
  "collections": {
    "policies": {
      "label": "Policies",
      "description": "Standing work the tower starts on a schedule: one markdown file each, a `# Title`, a ```json header, then the prompt. `tower x policies list` lists them."
    }
  },
  "streams": {
    "runs": {
      "scope": "project",
      "description": "Each policy's runs and passes, oldest first: kept in the folder runs/.",
      "facts": {
        "r": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "policy",
              "hash",
              "id",
              "start",
              "slot"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "policy": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "hash": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "id": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "by": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "check": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "exit": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": -9007199254740991,
                        "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                        "description": "Its exit code: 0, there is work; 1, none."
                      },
                      "ms": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 0,
                        "maximum": 9007199254740991
                      },
                      "out": {
                        "description": "Its stdout when it found work, at most 2,048 characters.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "maxLength": 2048
                      },
                      "stderr": {
                        "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "maxLength": 500
                      }
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "exit",
                      "ms"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "error": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "Why it has no exit code: it timed out, or could not start."
                      },
                      "ms": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 0,
                        "maximum": 9007199254740991
                      },
                      "stderr": {
                        "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "maxLength": 500
                      }
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "error",
                      "ms"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              "start": {
                "enum": [
                  "hand",
                  "auto",
                  "offer"
                ]
              },
              "slot": {
                "type": [
                  "string",
                  "null"
                ]
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "description": "A worker started for a policy: `slot` an ISO instant, null by hand."
        },
        "s": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "policy",
              "hash",
              "slot",
              "outcome"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "policy": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "hash": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "slot": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "outcome": {
                "enum": [
                  "offered",
                  "no-work",
                  "held",
                  "check-failed"
                ]
              },
              "check": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "exit": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": -9007199254740991,
                        "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                        "description": "Its exit code: 0, there is work; 1, none."
                      },
                      "ms": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 0,
                        "maximum": 9007199254740991
                      },
                      "out": {
                        "description": "Its stdout when it found work, at most 2,048 characters.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "maxLength": 2048
                      },
                      "stderr": {
                        "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "maxLength": 500
                      }
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "exit",
                      "ms"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "error": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "Why it has no exit code: it timed out, or could not start."
                      },
                      "ms": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 0,
                        "maximum": 9007199254740991
                      },
                      "stderr": {
                        "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                        "type": "string",
                        "maxLength": 500
                      }
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "error",
                      "ms"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "description": "A slot seen and not started, and why."
        }
      },
      "doors": {
        "read": "policies/runs/<project>",
        "append": "policies/run"
      }
    },
    "approvals": {
      "scope": "project",
      "description": "Each policy's approved hashes: kept in the folder approvals/.",
      "facts": {
        "a": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "policy",
              "hash"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "policy": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "hash": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "by": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "description": "A policy's hash approved for the runner to start on its own."
        }
      },
      "doors": {
        "read": "policies/runs/<project>",
        "append": "policies/approve"
      }
    }
  },
  "folds": {
    "card": {
      "x": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "run"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "run": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "policy",
              "tag",
              "n",
              "start",
              "slot"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "adds": [
        "lines",
        "badges"
      ]
    },
    "floor": {
      "x": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "policies",
          "offers"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "policies": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "id",
                "tag",
                "hash",
                "live",
                "calls",
                "actions"
              ]
            }
          },
          "offers": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "key",
                "project",
                "policy",
                "slot",
                "since",
                "until",
                "calls",
                "actions"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "adds": [
        "slots",
        "asks"
      ]
    }
  },
  "verbs": {
    "run": {
      "scope": "project",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "project": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[^./\\\\][^/\\\\]*$",
            "description": "The policy: its item's id in the project's `policies` collection."
          },
          "by": {
            "description": "The worker that makes the request, by session id: named on the run fact as the session that accepted or started it. Left out, the user makes it.",
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "check": {
            "description": "The check that let it run.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "exit": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": -9007199254740991,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                    "description": "Its exit code: 0, there is work; 1, none."
                  },
                  "ms": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 0,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991
                  },
                  "out": {
                    "description": "Its stdout when it found work, at most 2,048 characters.",
                    "type": "string",
                    "maxLength": 2048
                  },
                  "stderr": {
                    "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                    "type": "string",
                    "maxLength": 500
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "exit",
                  "ms"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false
              },
              {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "error": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Why it has no exit code: it timed out, or could not start."
                  },
                  "ms": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 0,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991
                  },
                  "stderr": {
                    "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                    "type": "string",
                    "maxLength": 500
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "error",
                  "ms"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false
              }
            ]
          },
          "start": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "hand",
              "auto",
              "offer"
            ],
            "description": "`hand`, now with no slot; `auto`, a runner at its slot; `offer`, an open offer accepted."
          },
          "slot": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
            "description": "The slot it runs for, epoch ms: one of the policy's, at or before now. Required by `auto` and `offer`; `hand` takes none."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "project",
          "policy",
          "start"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "t": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "ran"
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The worker's session."
          },
          "n": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": -9007199254740991,
            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
            "description": "The run's number among the policy's runs."
          },
          "hash": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "t",
          "id",
          "n",
          "hash"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "description": "Start a run of a policy: its file parsed now, a worker spawned on its prose with its `hire`, and a run fact appended to the project's `runs` stream (a worker whose fact can't be appended is killed). It needs no approval (the caller consents), except `auto`, refused unless the file's words as read now are approved. Refused for an invalid policy, another runner's, a slot already run, or the host down; `limited` while as many of its runs run as its `live`. A policy's runs, passes and approvals are taken one at a time.",
      "words": {
        "label": "Run now",
        "hint": "start a run of the policy now"
      }
    },
    "run-now": {
      "scope": "project",
      "description": "Start a policy now, named by its tag or id: its open offer's slot when it has one, else by hand. `run` is the same for a caller that holds the policy's call, as a renderer does.",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "project": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "description": "The policy: its tag or its id."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "project",
          "policy"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "t": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "ran"
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The worker's session."
          },
          "n": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The run's number among the policy's runs."
          },
          "hash": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "said": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What it came to, in words."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "t",
          "id",
          "n",
          "hash",
          "said"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "cli": {
        "positional": [
          "policy"
        ],
        "print": "said",
        "usage": "run-now <policy>"
      }
    },
    "pass": {
      "scope": "project",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "project": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[^./\\\\][^/\\\\]*$",
            "description": "The policy: its item's id in the project's `policies` collection."
          },
          "slot": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
            "description": "One of the policy's slots, epoch ms, at or before now."
          },
          "outcome": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "offered",
              "no-work",
              "held",
              "check-failed"
            ]
          },
          "check": {
            "description": "The check, when one ran.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "exit": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": -9007199254740991,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                    "description": "Its exit code: 0, there is work; 1, none."
                  },
                  "ms": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 0,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991
                  },
                  "out": {
                    "description": "Its stdout when it found work, at most 2,048 characters.",
                    "type": "string",
                    "maxLength": 2048
                  },
                  "stderr": {
                    "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                    "type": "string",
                    "maxLength": 500
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "exit",
                  "ms"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false
              },
              {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "error": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Why it has no exit code: it timed out, or could not start."
                  },
                  "ms": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 0,
                    "maximum": 9007199254740991
                  },
                  "stderr": {
                    "description": "The end of its stderr when it failed, at most 500 characters.",
                    "type": "string",
                    "maxLength": 500
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "error",
                  "ms"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "project",
          "policy",
          "slot",
          "outcome"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "t": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "ok"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "t"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "description": "Record a slot of a policy the runner saw and didn't start, and why: `offered`, `no-work`, `held` (live was full), `check-failed`. Refused once the slot has a fact."
    },
    "approve": {
      "scope": "project",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "project": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[^./\\\\][^/\\\\]*$",
            "description": "The policy: its item's id in the project's `policies` collection."
          },
          "hash": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$",
            "description": "The hash of the policy's file as the approver read it, `sha256:<hex>`."
          },
          "by": {
            "description": "The worker that makes the request, by session id: named on the approval fact. Left out, the user makes it.",
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "project",
          "policy",
          "hash"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "t": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "ok"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "t"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "description": "Approve a policy's current words for the runner to start on its own (`start: auto`): refused unless `hash` is the file's hash now. Any edit needs a new approval.",
      "words": {
        "label": "Approve",
        "hint": "approve the policy's words as they are now, for it to start on its own"
      }
    },
    "approve-now": {
      "scope": "project",
      "description": "Approve a policy's words as they are now, named by its tag or id. `approve` is the same for a caller that holds the hash it read, as a renderer does.",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "project": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "description": "The policy: its tag or its id."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "project",
          "policy"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "t": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "ok"
          },
          "said": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What it came to, in words."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "t",
          "said"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "cli": {
        "positional": [
          "policy"
        ],
        "print": "said",
        "usage": "approve-now <policy>"
      }
    }
  },
  "reads": {
    "runs/<project>": {
      "scope": "project",
      "query": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[^./\\\\][^/\\\\]*$",
            "description": "The policy: its item's id in the project's `policies` collection."
          },
          "limit": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^([1-9][0-9]{0,2}|1000)$",
            "description": "How many of its latest runs, newest first: 20 when left out, at most 1000."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "policy"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "n",
            "slot",
            "at",
            "hash",
            "current",
            "start",
            "worker"
          ]
        }
      },
      "description": "A policy's runs, newest first: each run's number, slot, how it started and on which hash, its check, and its worker as it is now, its latest answer in full."
    },
    "said/<project>": {
      "scope": "project",
      "description": "What the CLI prints of the floor's policies, in this extension's words: each policy's lines and where it stands, by id, and with `policy`, its latest `runs` runs.",
      "query": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A policy's id: its runs' lines too."
          },
          "runs": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^([1-9][0-9]{0,2}|1000)$",
            "description": "How many of its latest runs: 5 when left out."
          }
        }
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "lines",
          "standing"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "lines": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "standing": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "runs": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "list/<project>": {
      "scope": "project",
      "description": "The floor's policies in words: each one's rule, approval, live runs, last run and where it stands now.",
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "lines"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "lines": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "cli": {
        "word": "list",
        "print": "lines"
      }
    },
    "run-lines/<project>": {
      "scope": "project",
      "description": "A policy's latest runs in words, newest first: each with its worker, what it showed and its latest answer cut short. No policy named, the one the caller is a run of.",
      "query": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The policy: its tag or its id. Left out, the one the caller is a run of."
          },
          "limit": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^([1-9][0-9]{0,2}|1000)$",
            "description": "How many of its latest runs: 5 when left out, 20 at most."
          }
        }
      },
      "reply": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "lines"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "lines": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "cli": {
        "word": "runs",
        "positional": [
          "policy"
        ],
        "print": "lines",
        "usage": "runs [<policy>] [--limit <n>]"
      }
    }
  },
  "guidance": {
    "brief": "Standing work the tower starts on a schedule: write one with `tower keep policies`, see where each stands with `tower x policies list`.",
    "full": "A policy is standing work the floor keeps in its `policies` collection: one markdown file, a `# Title`, a fenced json header (when it fires, whether each slot is offered to the user or started on its own, how many runs may run at once, where its worker starts), then the prose that is the worker's whole prompt.\n\nUse it when the user asks about work that recurs: what is scheduled, when something next runs, why it did or didn't start, or to set something up to run on its own. Not for one-off work: hire a worker for that.\n\n- `tower x policies list`: each policy's rule in words, its approval, its live runs, its last run and where it stands now, the same reason the tower acts on. `needs you` means a run on duty holds a slot: end that run for the next slot to start.\n- `tower x policies run-now <tag>`: starts it now, or takes its open offer.\n- `tower x policies approve-now <tag>`: approves its words as they are now. Approving is the user's: read it first with `tower read <tag>`, and don't approve unless asked.\n- `tower x policies runs [<tag>] [--limit <n>]`: a policy's latest runs, each with its worker, what it showed and its latest answer cut short (5 unless told, 20 at most). `tower agent <CALLSIGN>` reads one in full.\n\nThe tag is the first column of `list`. `run`, `pass` and `approve` are the renderers' calls, which take a slot or a hash: use the words above.\n\nWrite a policy with `tower keep policies` (markdown on stdin) and edit it in place; an edit to the words of an auto policy needs the user's approval again.\n\nWhen you are a run, `tower whoami` says which policy and slot you are, and `tower x policies runs` lists what earlier runs did and left: read it before you start, and end with what the next run needs to know. The handbook's Policies section has the header's keys."
  }
}
